From: Codex M2 runtime compatibility
Subject: [PATCH] Match A376B cameraserver ABI and recognize OneUI80500 in legacy Camera

Reason: runtime S22 cameraserver cannot resolve AudioSystem::streamTypeToAttributes,
and static closure also finds an incompatible OutputConfiguration constructor.
Use hash-pinned native A37 cameraserver, porting only the existing 8-byte zero
max-buffer fallback. Retained Camera APK crashes on exact version80500; map only
that value to its existing V8_0 feature set, preserving unknown-version errors.
Files: native camera finalization and two reviewed Python adapters. M2/A376B/
star2lte only. No audio-library, kernel, vendor hardware blob or system-version
property replacement. Proprietary binaries remain outside the patch.
Verify: donor/instruction hashes, unchanged server remainder, wrong-input rejection,
shell syntax and profile scope; compiled APK changes classes3.dex only, retains
resource/native bytes and signer; actual G965F boot/Enforcing, native service
stability, device enumeration and Camera launch. Preview/photo acceptance is
separate from successful service startup. See docs/m2-camera-metadata-fixes.md.
Rollback: reverse patch/rebuild or restore exact original server/APK on test device.

